WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.100
Jeremy Renner's snow plow accident was&nbsp;
shocking to say the least — and now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.280
the star himself has given fans&nbsp;
an update about his condition.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.620
Renner took to Instagram on Tuesday, January&nbsp;
3rd, to offer up his very first message to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.580
the public since his serious snow plow&nbsp;
accident. The star has been described&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.320
as being in "critical but stable" condition&nbsp;
following an accident involving a snow plow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.180
on January 1st. Police officials say Renner&nbsp;
was near Mt. Rose Highway in Reno, Nevada,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.620
when the accident occurred, and that he&nbsp;
suffered a serious injury to his chest.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:36.000
"As Mr. Renner always does on those private&nbsp;
roads, he was being a great neighbor and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.180
was plowing those roads for his neighbors,&nbsp;
because, as I say, they had three feet."

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.080
It was subsequently reported that&nbsp;
Renner underwent surgery for blunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.760
chest trauma and orthopedic injuries. A&nbsp;
representative sent out a statement, saying:

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.200
"Jeremy's family would like to express&nbsp;
their gratitude to the incredible doctors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.580
and nurses looking after him [...] They&nbsp;
are also tremendously overwhelmed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.300
appreciative of the outpouring of&nbsp;
love and support from his fans."

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.200
While things have appeared to be proceeding&nbsp;
smoothly with Renner's treatment and the start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.220
of his recovery, many fans have nonetheless&nbsp;
been anxious to hear more about how the star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:12.600
is doing. Thankfully, it now seems that&nbsp;
the actor has recovered enough to manage a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:17.700
reassuring personal update on his own wellbeing,&nbsp;
as well as a heartfelt thank you to everyone via&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.500
social media. This has prompted a deluge of&nbsp;
support in the comments on his Instagram page.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.640
In the new post, the actor included a&nbsp;
single photo of himself in the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.000
in which he is severely bruised and hooked up to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.140
medical equipment — nevertheless very&nbsp;
much alive. In a caption, he wrote:

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:39.360
"Thank you all for your kind words. I'm too messed&nbsp;
up now to type. But I send love to you all."

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.580
An update from Renner himself has proven to&nbsp;
be a moment of comfort for fans in what has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.680
otherwise been an uneasy and concerning series&nbsp;
of updates regarding the actor's condition. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:57.360
post garnered a startling amount of attention,&nbsp;
amassing more than 5,700,000 likes and 230,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.760
comments within roughly 18 hours of being posted.&nbsp;
While the actor remains in critical condition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:07.500
it hopefully won't be too long before fans&nbsp;
get another update about Renner's recovery.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:10.020
Not long after Renner broke&nbsp;
his silence on the 3rd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:14.400
fans started flocking to his post&nbsp;
to show support. One fan commented:

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.720
"Happy to see you awake."

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.560
Another said:

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.820
"Was really worried about you even if we&nbsp;
don't know each other. Get well soon."

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.260
Another fan commented:

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.760
"Thinking of you every day man, sending&nbsp;
love and prayers to my favorite hero."

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:29.280
Many fans were quick to invoke Renner's role as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.920
Hawkeye in the MCU in their&nbsp;
well-wishes. As one said:

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.620
"Get better Hawkeye, we all&nbsp;
send our love &amp; support."

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:38.700
Many of Renner's colleagues from throughout&nbsp;
the film and entertainment industry also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:42.420
took the time to comment on the post.&nbsp;
Fellow Marvel star Chris Pratt said:

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:44.520
"Continued prayers your way brutha."

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.500
Meanwhile, Vanessa Hudgens wrote:

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.080
"Sending so much love [and] healing!"

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.120
And actor Tasha Smith declared:

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.960
"[You're] a tough mother you know&nbsp;
what and I love you for it all!"

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:59.580
In addition to showing support, many users&nbsp;
and celebrities expressed their happiness that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:05.160
Renner was well enough to provide his own update.&nbsp;
Celebrity trainer and actor Jason Walsh posted:

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:08.760
"Damn brother I was really worried&nbsp;
about you. Good to see your face."

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.060
And Renner's Tag co-star Isla Fisher commented:

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:19.140
"Phew! I'm so happy you made this post. Sending&nbsp;
you so much love and healing energy. We love you."

